Installation is as on other MikroTik devices. In summary, permanent installation occurs in two steps:
  - Boot an initramfs image over TFTP.
  - Flash the final image using ''sysupgrade''.

The RouterOS 7 bootloader is not compatible with OpenWrt. If a device is running the RouterOS 7 bootloader, [[toh:mikrotik:common##make_sure_the_bootloader_is_compatible|downgrade it to RouterOS 6 and flash the bootloader]] before installing OpenWrt.

===== Basic configuration =====

After flashing, proceed with [[docs:guide-user:base-system:start|basic configuration]] to set up the Internet connection, configure wireless, etc.

===== Specific configuration =====

==== Network interfaces ====

The default network configuration:

^ Interface Name ^ Case Label ^ Description ^ Default configuration ^
| ''br-lan'' | | LAN | 192.168.1.1/24 |
| ''eth0'' | | CPU GMAC, connected to switch | None |
| ''sw-eth1'' | ETH1 | Switch port, accepts PoE In | Bridged to ''br-lan'' |
| ''sw-eth2'' | ETH2 | Switch port | Bridged to ''br-lan'' |
| ''phy0-ap0'' | | WiFi, 2.4GHz 802.11b/g/n | Disabled; bridged to ''br-lan'' |
| ''phy1-ap0'' | | WiFi, 5GHz 802.11a/n/ac | Disabled; bridged to ''br-lan'' |

==== Buttons ====

^ Button Name ^ Case Label ^ Event ^
| Reset | RESET | ''reset'' |

==== LEDs ====

^ LED Name ^ Case Label ^ Color ^ Internal name ^ Use ^
| Power | PWR | ''blue:power'' | Blue | Keep state from bootloader (expected on when powered) |
| User | USR | ''green:user'' | Green | Diag indicator: blink patterns for ''boot'', ''failsafe'', and ''upgrade'' states; solid in ''running'' state |

ETH1 and ETH2 also have one green and one amber LED each, but they are configured to remain under switch control to show link/activity (green) and speed (amber), and are not under OpenWrt’s control.

-> Generic [[docs:guide-user:base-system:led_configuration|LED configuration documentation]].

===== Hardware =====

==== Info ====  
^ Architecture | ARMv7 (32-bit) |
^ Vendor | Qualcomm |
^ Bootloader | RouterBoot |
^ System-On-Chip | Qualcomm IPQ4018 |
^ CPU/Speed | Qualcomm IPQ4018 (SoC integrated), 4x 716 MHz |
^ CPU Implementation | Cortex-A7 with NEON and VPFv4 |
^ Flash-Chip | Winbond W25Q128JVSM |
^ Flash size | 16 MiB |
^ RAM | 128 MiB |
^ Wireless | Qualcomm IPQ4018 (SoC integrated), 2.4GHz 802.11b/g/n, 5GHz 802.11a/n/ac |
^ Wi-Fi Generation | 2.4GHz -> WiFi 4, 5GHz -> Wi-Fi 5 |
^ Ethernet | 2x 10/100/1000 Mbit/s, VLAN support |
^ Switch | Qualcomm IPQ4018 (SoC integrated) |
^ USB | No |
^ Serial | Yes, via pads on board |
^ Powering | DC jack 10–57V, PoE-in 802.3af/at or 10–57V |
^ Ingress Protection | IP54 |

